{"id":"davco-sanitized-colorgrout","rules":[{"id":"davco-sanitized-colorgrout:suitability:fbfa4717","type":"suitability","polarity":"yes","conditional":false,"tags":{"tile_type":["ceramic","natural_stone"]},"mentions":[],"text":"A premium cementitious grout designed for use with most types of ceramic tiles and natural stone applications","heading":"DESCRIPTION","source":{"doc_type":"PDS","url":"https://aus.sika.com/content/dam/dms/au01/0/davco-sanitized-colorgrout.pdf","page":1,"page_end":1,"doc_version":"April 2025, Version 01.02","section":"DESCRIPTION","web_url":"https://aus.sika.com/en/construction/tile-stone-installationsystems/tile-grouts/davco-sanitized-colorgrout.html"}},{"id":"davco-sanitized-colorgrout:suitability:4ddc4a06","type":"suitability","polarity":"yes","conditional":false,"tags":{"environment":["external","internal"]},"mentions":[],"text":"Suitable for interior and exterior applications","heading":"USES","source":{"doc_type":"PDS","url":"https://aus.sika.com/content/dam/dms/au01/0/davco-sanitized-colorgrout.pdf","page":1,"page_end":1,"doc_version":"April 2025, Version 01.02","section":"USES","web_url":"https://aus.sika.com/en/construction/tile-stone-installationsystems/tile-grouts/davco-sanitized-colorgrout.html"}},{"id":"davco-sanitized-colorgrout:suitability:cf993054","type":"suitability","polarity":"no","conditional":false,"tags":{"environment":["commercial"]},"mentions":[],"text":"It is not suitable for use in harsh and demanding environments or where there are hygienic requirements i.e. commercial kitchens, public toilets, food processing plants etc","heading":"USES","source":{"doc_type":"PDS","url":"https://aus.sika.com/content/dam/dms/au01/0/davco-sanitized-colorgrout.pdf","page":1,"page_end":1,"doc_version":"April 2025, Version 01.02","section":"USES","web_url":"https://aus.sika.com/en/construction/tile-stone-installationsystems/tile-grouts/davco-sanitized-colorgrout.html"}},{"id":"davco-sanitized-colorgrout:suitability:82d4b971","type":"suitability","polarity":"yes","conditional":false,"tags":{"substrate":["epoxy_coating"]},"mentions":[],"text":"use a suitable Sika epoxy tile grout.","heading":"USES","source":{"doc_type":"PDS","url":"https://aus.sika.com/content/dam/dms/au01/0/davco-sanitized-colorgrout.pdf","page":1,"page_end":1,"doc_version":"April 2025, Version 01.02","section":"USES","web_url":"https://aus.sika.com/en/construction/tile-stone-installationsystems/tile-grouts/davco-sanitized-colorgrout.html"}},{"id":"davco-sanitized-colorgrout:suitability:d76d75ca","type":"suitability","polarity":"yes","conditional":false,"tags":{"environment":["submerged","wet_area"]},"mentions":[],"text":"Ideal for dry and wet areas including swimming pools and spas","heading":"CHARACTERISTICS / ADVANTAGES","source":{"doc_type":"PDS","url":"https://aus.sika.com/content/dam/dms/au01/0/davco-sanitized-colorgrout.pdf","page":1,"page_end":1,"doc_version":"April 2025, Version 01.02","section":"CHARACTERISTICS / ADVANTAGES","web_url":"https://aus.sika.com/en/construction/tile-stone-installationsystems/tile-grouts/davco-sanitized-colorgrout.html"}},{"id":"davco-sanitized-colorgrout:restriction:37e8873c","type":"restriction","polarity":"no","conditional":false,"tags":{},"mentions":[],"text":"Do not apply in temperatures above 35°C or below 5°C","heading":"IMPORTANT CONSIDERATIONS","source":{"doc_type":"PDS","url":"https://aus.sika.com/content/dam/dms/au01/0/davco-sanitized-colorgrout.pdf","page":2,"page_end":2,"doc_version":"April 2025, Version 01.02","section":"IMPORTANT CONSIDERATIONS","web_url":"https://aus.sika.com/en/construction/tile-stone-installationsystems/tile-grouts/davco-sanitized-colorgrout.html"}},{"id":"davco-sanitized-colorgrout:suitability:49deafc2","type":"suitability","polarity":"no","conditional":false,"tags":{"environment":["commercial"]},"mentions":[],"text":"Davco® Sanitized Colorgrout is not suitable for use in harsh and demanding environments or where there are hygienic requirements i.e. commercial kitchens, public toilets, food processing plants etc","heading":"IMPORTANT CONSIDERATIONS","source":{"doc_type":"PDS","url":"https://aus.sika.com/content/dam/dms/au01/0/davco-sanitized-colorgrout.pdf","page":2,"page_end":2,"doc_version":"April 2025, Version 01.02","section":"IMPORTANT CONSIDERATIONS","web_url":"https://aus.sika.com/en/construction/tile-stone-installationsystems/tile-grouts/davco-sanitized-colorgrout.html"}},{"id":"davco-sanitized-colorgrout:restriction:7255b9d2","type":"restriction","polarity":"no","conditional":false,"tags":{},"mentions":[],"text":"Do not apply Davco® Sanitized Colorgrout in movement joints","heading":"IMPORTANT CONSIDERATIONS","source":{"doc_type":"PDS","url":"https://aus.sika.com/content/dam/dms/au01/0/davco-sanitized-colorgrout.pdf","page":2,"page_end":2,"doc_version":"April 2025, Version 01.02","section":"IMPORTANT CONSIDERATIONS","web_url":"https://aus.sika.com/en/construction/tile-stone-installationsystems/tile-grouts/davco-sanitized-colorgrout.html"}},{"id":"davco-sanitized-colorgrout:restriction:69ce5f3d","type":"restriction","polarity":"no","conditional":false,"tags":{},"mentions":[],"text":"Do not apply neat or strong acids on Sanitized® Colorgrouts.","heading":"IMPORTANT CONSIDERATIONS","source":{"doc_type":"PDS","url":"https://aus.sika.com/content/dam/dms/au01/0/davco-sanitized-colorgrout.pdf","page":2,"page_end":2,"doc_version":"April 2025, Version 01.02","section":"IMPORTANT CONSIDERATIONS","web_url":"https://aus.sika.com/en/construction/tile-stone-installationsystems/tile-grouts/davco-sanitized-colorgrout.html"}},{"id":"davco-sanitized-colorgrout:primer:7053b58d","type":"primer","polarity":"yes","conditional":true,"tags":{},"mentions":["davco-4-in-1-groutadditive"],"text":"If the tiles are particularly porous it is advisable to prime the joints with Davco 4 in 1 Grout Additive after dampening to seal the edge of the tile. 1. Using a rubber float or squeegee work the grout into the joints in a diagonal motion making sure that the grout does not just sit on top of the joint i.e. the grout does not bridge the joint. 2. Remove excess grout from the surface of the tiles with the rubber float or squeegee using a diagonal motion. 3. Use a damp sponge to clean up the remainder of the grout","heading":"APPLICATION","source":{"doc_type":"PDS","url":"https://aus.sika.com/content/dam/dms/au01/0/davco-sanitized-colorgrout.pdf","page":3,"page_end":3,"doc_version":"April 2025, Version 01.02","section":"APPLICATION","web_url":"https://aus.sika.com/en/construction/tile-stone-installationsystems/tile-grouts/davco-sanitized-colorgrout.html"}}]}